          automatically.  Build clean, smoke clean.  USER VISUAL
          CONFIRMATION PENDING (pedestal scroll).
          STAIRSTEP SUBDIVISION (implemented then reverted with the
          above): vanilla stairstep tries a full axis or nothing,
          dropping a whole axis for a tic on grazing corners (the
          captured bump: graze intercept frac 0.047 -> flush fails ->
          stairstep-y kept 0 x-motion).  The reverted version ended
          slidemove with trysubdiv per axis (binary search to first
          contact, 6 rounds to 1/64, both axes always attempted);
          replay of the incident tic preserved x at 63/64 instead
          of 0.  Removed; slide flush/retry logic was untouched
          throughout (vanilla-exact).
          DOOR SLICE (milestone 13 first cut): use-lines + manual
